Z||000004||Monkeyman||01-21-2000||05:56 PM||||I emailed Tom a while back about his headlight conversion.  He said that there was a Lexan (I think) cover for it.  Also, make sure that the round lights in the pic are legal.  Some of the round light conversions use driving lights which are not only illegal, but dangerous IMHO.  Tom uses "real" headlights.  Toms' kit runs $170US last time I checked his site.  His site is at:  <A HREF="http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/tomfiero/" TARGET=_blank>www.digitalfusion.on.ca/tomfiero/</A>  <BR>His site is part of Darklords site which will be upgraded shortly.  Look for something from him in the future.  I don't want to give anything away, but let's just say that Darklords future's so bright, he has to wear shades!<p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 01-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||V6pack||01-21-2000||09:21 PM||||To all:  I spoke by phone today with the Virginia based Gary's custom owner.  His bulbs are 55 watt each, low beam only set up.  He said you could increase the wattage.  He will not/can not sell the covers seperately.<P>I also e-mailed Tom today and he replied very quickly, (thanks Tom) and said he has a template for a lense cover, but had not yet had time to produce the covers yet.<P>I too would like the rectangular light with a high/low function like Tom's with the lens covers over them.<P>I suppose they could be cut out and a moulding put on the edges, and attached by a good man with tools. That is the up to date scoop...<P>V6pack||||reg||10
Z||000006||TOM||01-21-2000||11:49 PM||||You Rang. I dont know about gary's. I have never spoken to him or asked about info. But I think the price is $300 or more. And you say you only get low beams. My kits are $170 without the covers and $190 with them. I tried to make them lower but its the cost of the light that makes them that high. With mine. The low beam is the outers and the high is all four. They are all 55w bulbs but can be upgraded to 85w with readily available bulbs from any local auto parts store. They are easilt replacable. I wouldnt go any higher with the bulbs with covers on because of the heat they generate. I have seen bulbs as high as 105w that will fit||||reg||1
Z||000007||TOM||01-21-2000||11:55 PM||||I went to gary's site and whew. I think the light kit requires some modification. Im nit sure but it says comre with all breackes and hardware.<BR>and $139 for trans am hood vents or $229 for thunderbird turbo coupe hood vents. Thats just plain rude.At $325 for the tail light mod I think I will try to make some of those to see how cheap I can offer them||||reg||1
Z||000008||TOM||01-21-2000||11:58 PM||||Geezo peezo. $205 for power windows and $105 for locks. My prices are less than half of that and I use all fiero parts not some universal kit ||||reg||1
Z||000009||BigBoyToys||01-22-2000||12:16 AM||||Tom,<BR>I really like the idea of this conversion particularly the fact that yours requires little to no mods. My only concern is the light pattern and getting light to my perefrial (sides). I live in deer country and  I gotta see them before they see me. It seems that with the lights set down and in you would loose much of that light. Have you done any nightime side by side comparisons. Or do the lenses compensate for this some how?||||reg||5
Z||000010||V6pack||01-22-2000||12:26 AM||||Tom, I talked to him just before I wrote to you.  He says it is an "L bracket" hardware install. Too much $ for me!<P>On the tail light panels.  I have aset of PISA'a on my T-top. They are not much fun to work with, but come out okay. The full Vette lights are not necessary. Of course I didn't find that out until I popped for a good set of '82's at $35.X4.<P>I found the perfect lenses that make the job way easier and much cheaper. <P>If you are going to market that product I probably shouldn't blab here unless you want me to, and if you want I can e-mail this alternative to you. <P>But, there are a lot of tail light lenses out there that will fit PISA's panels. Gary's panel looks slightly hooded above the lenses...nice touch.<P>With these inexpensive lenses and reasonably priced panels you could do the mod for just a little bit more than you will get for your surplus GT tail lights on eBay.<BR>V6pack||||reg||12
