Z||000024||GREENDANO||01-23-2000||11:03 AM||||As far as New York State inspection/legality goes....  (that's where I live, and I'm a NYS licensed inspector)  It illegal to alter any OEM lighting system.  Plus, headlights can't have any covers over them that aren't OEM.. i.e. smoke tint covers or clear covers that have been painted with graphics.  <BR>  Have I altered my lights before?  Yes.  People that know my 85 GT have seen it has the PISA conversion.  Would I alter other lights?  Yes.  Just make sure they look cleanly installed, and are firmly mounted and aimed correctly.  If they are DOT approved lights and not just a set of fog/driving lights, you might get away with it if the guy looking at your car doesn't know Fieros.  <BR>  Tom, your conversion looks cool.  Do you use Camaro parts, or copies of Camaro parts or is it just me?  <BR>  There's my $0.03 worth  (price adjusted for inflation)<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||1
Z||000025||Monkeyman||01-23-2000||12:12 PM||||Some of us don't have to worry about inspections.  Yeehaw!  I can do anything I want to my Fiero and nobody will say a word.  Let's see...dark tint, no cat (he!!.  No mufflers for that matter!), Toms head light kit, lowered, turbo on the 2.8 (just cause it'll look cool!).  The sky's (and my wife checkbook) the limit!!||||reg||1
